2026-11-10  ebeem  <lord.ebeem@gmail.com>
	Version 0.0.5 released.

	BREAKING CHANGES:
	* removed (gliver contrib ui statusbar), if it's imported in user
	configuration then it should be removed. (gliver contrib ui gleui)
	already imports it.

	UPDATES:
	* gleui/toast: Add #:eat-next-key? key to emit toast on next key
	press.
	* commands/help: Add describe-top-map command to show the
	keybindings available under the top-map.
	* contrib/keybindings: Add the keybindings s-SPC h ? to show the
	top-map keybindings.
	* gleui/palette: Fix a problem where the last focused window isn't
	automatically focused after the palette is closed.
	* river/viewporter-manager: Implement Wayland viewporter protocol
	to support fractional scaling.
	* river/fractional-scale-manager: Implement Wayland protocol
	fractional-scale-v1 to support fractional scaling of UI.
	* commands/shell: Fix gliver-quit command and introduce config
	parameter *quit-exits-river* to exit only Gliver or river
	completly.
	* river/*: Add more guard checks and improve tracking of created
	and destroyed objects.
	* core/types: Drop the function (seat-current) as there's no
	actual concept of current seat in Wayland. Having such a function
	will most likely cause errors in the future.
	* core/surface: Add core module surface to provide fractional
	scaling information.
	* gleui/palette: Fix Wayland keyboard is cached in palette causing
	it to become unresponsive if seat is re-created.
	* core/config: Use different suffix for state (repl & logs) if the
	use Wayland display is different than wayland-1 (avoid conflicts).
	* core/helpers: Improve define-var macro to introduce key
	#:inherit which allows variable inheritance.
	* gleui/*: Fix Wayland pointer is cached causing it to become
	unresponsive if seat is re-created.
	* gleui/widgets: Implement simple declarative framework (flutter
	inspired) to create common UI widgets.
	* gleui/*: Refactor gleui components to utilize gleui refactored
	base and widgets.
	* gleui/statusbar: Switch bar layout from stack to flex row, this
	should help prevent them from overlapping.
	* gleui/toast: Make toast accept a gleui-widget rather than the
	custom row/column records.
	* ui/components: Remove backend wrappers and call gleui UI
	components directly. This wrappers were meant to abstract these
	components which should allow users to use other backends for them
	like fuzzel or rofi. This is not in the vision anymore.
	* core/config: All palette definitions starting with `*palette-`
	moved to (gliver contrib ui gleui palette), users who overwrite
	these variables will have to import the module or use var-set!
	instead.
	* gleui/statusbar: statusbar modules are now under the same
	directory as the gleui statusbar module, there is no plan to make
	the statusbar modules backend-agnostic.
	* gleui/statusbar: statusbar modules update functions now all run
	in a background worker to avoid main thread blocking.

